From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 08:26:38 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] backend-drm: offer LINEAR on a KMS device without
 modifiers

On a KMS device without IN_FORMATS -- QEMU's virtio-gpu, whose driver
takes no modifiers in AddFB2 -- each plane format gets only
DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID, and that is all the scanout tranche of the
dma-buf feedback offers. But drm_fb_get_from_dmabuf() never puts an
implicit-modifier buffer on a plane, so a client that reallocates from
the scanout tranche is refused again ("couldn't get FB for view: 0x4",
DMABUF_MODIFIER_INVALID) and its window stays composed by the GPU.

Such a driver takes a linear buffer: drm_fb_addfb() imports it through
the legacy AddFB2 when the device has no modifier support. Add LINEAR
to the plane formats in that case, after INVALID, so the renderer's own
gbm surface is allocated as before and a client can pick LINEAR from
the scanout tranche.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/libweston/backend-drm/kms.c
+++ b/libweston/backend-drm/kms.c
@@ -594,6 +594,17 @@
 		ret = weston_drm_format_add_modifier(fmt, DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID);
 		if (ret < 0)
 			return -1;
+		/* A driver that takes no modifiers in AddFB2 takes a linear
+		 * buffer through the legacy entry point (drm_fb_addfb), so say
+		 * so: a client that reallocates from the scanout tranche can
+		 * then pick LINEAR, while an implicit-modifier buffer is never
+		 * scanned out (drm_fb_get_from_dmabuf). */
+		if (!use_modifiers) {
+			ret = weston_drm_format_add_modifier(fmt,
+							     DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR);
+			if (ret < 0)
+				return -1;
+		}
 	}
 	return 0;
 }
